{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== STATUS: ALL THIS STORY'S OWN TEST DEFECTS ARE NOW FIXED AND MERGED. ONE PRODUCT BUG REMAINS,\nAND IT IS OWNED ELSEWHERE. ===\n\nMERGED (Gerrit 1214, 1215, 1216, submitted as a stack; content verified on gerrit/main afterwards\nbecause Gerrit rebases on submit):\n  * 1214 'pin the outbound DC status routing defect'\n  * 1215 'localise the inbound-link skip, fix the assignee oracle'\n  * 1216 'mutation-check the rewritten assignee oracle'\n4 files, 536 insertions. NOTE for whoever pushes next from a fresh worktree: these three commits\nwere authored WITHOUT Change-Ids (the fresh worktree lacked the commit-msg hook) and Gerrit would\nhave rejected them; they were stamped by re-running the hook via\n'git rebase origin/main --exec \"git commit --amend --no-edit\"' and the content was confirmed\nbyte-identical afterwards. Install the hook when you create the worktree.\n\n--- THE SIX HARNESS FAILURES, RE-TRIAGED AGAINST WHAT IS NOW ON MAIN ---\n\n1. INBOUND LINK CELL — NOT A PRODUCT DEFECT, and this is the important correction. The cell that\n   failed in run 30731818113 was the PRE-PRIMING version of test_inbound_link_round_trips; the\n   priming pass was added later by ae009443a9 (ticket b9b8), so NO harness run has ever exercised\n   the current cell. The CI log shows set_relationship called immediately after\n   _jira_key_to_local_id with no pass between, and 'git show 338e397335:...' confirms it.\n   The underlying skip is real but STRUCTURAL and correct-by-phase-order: inbound_differ.py:402-404\n   skips an unbound counterpart and :409-412 skips one absent from local_tickets_by_id, which is\n   built once from ctx.local_tickets at reconcile.py:250 — while run_differs runs the inbound differ\n   at :239 BEFORE the binding walk at :240, and applier.apply not until reconcile.py:454. So on the\n   pass that first sees the target the link cannot land, and it lands on the next one. Pinned by\n   tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_lands_locally_5200.py (6 cells, no live\n   Jira): bound+present emits the add; unbound-only emits nothing; bound-but-locally-absent emits\n   nothing; the far-end mirror emits the inverse. The POSITIVE case is what makes the two empty\n   results evidence rather than absence.\n   Two upstream suspects were checked and REJECTED rather than assumed: get_issuelinks_map's\n   fields=None does NOT mean 'no fields' (pycontribs jira/client.py:3619-3620 converts it to\n   ['*all']), and outbound link-REMOVE suppression cannot fire because a DC-created link is\n   never-managed (outbound_links.py:112-116). The applier half was verified working end to end.\n   NO BUG FILED — deliberately, because there is no product defect here.\n\n2. OUTBOUND TRANSITION-STATUS — A REAL P1 PRODUCT DEFECT, now [rebar:d067-5d2f-bcee-46ae] (child of\n   e369, claimed, fix in progress). 7f93 does NOT cover it: the outbound path never calls\n   transition_issue_by_name at all. adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:248-255 pops only\n   'assignee' and puts everything else into issue.update(fields=kwargs) — a REST field edit — while\n   Cloud's adapters/jira/acli.py:170,182-183 pops 'status' and routes it to transition_issue.\n   Jira rejects a status field edit, it is soft-failed, the pass exits 0, and the status silently\n   never changes. Characterization test now on main proves it: edited_fields ==\n   [{'status': 'In Progress'}] with transitions_probed == [] — NO transitions probe happens at all,\n   which rules out 'attempted and rejected'. THIS CELL WILL KEEP FAILING UNTIL d067 LANDS. That is\n   correct behaviour from the cell; do not touch it here.\n\n3. INBOUND ASSIGNEE — THIS STORY'S OWN TEST DEFECT, FIXED (1215/1216). The oracle compared\n   ensure_identity_for's return against itself, which can never fail. It now observes the identity\n   REGISTRY across the pass via the read-only rebar.resolve_mapping: absent BEFORE (stated as a\n   setup assertion), resolving AFTER, is_placeholder, and resolve_mapping('jira-datacenter', ...)\n   is None so the family is asserted in BOTH directions. Mutation-checked in\n   test_inbound_assignee_oracle_discriminates_5200.py: RED is reachable (resolve_mapping returns\n   None twice on an unminted store, so a lazily-creating implementation would restore the\n   tautology) and GREEN is reachable FOR THE RIGHT REASON, driven through the production\n   _ensure_inbound_assignee_identity with a DC-shaped user object carrying no accountId.\n\n4. INBOUND EDIT-SUMMARY — fixed by b9b8 (merged ae009443a9).\n5. IDEMPOTENCE / PHANTOM OUTBOUND UPDATE — fixed by [rebar:727f-b351-59ba-4b3b], CLOSED.\n6. SNAPSHOT-ABSENT KEY PLANNED AS CREATE — fixed by [rebar:d103-c3f8-2fbc-4c97], CLOSED.\n\n--- LIVE EVIDENCE IN FLIGHT ---\nHarness run 30763838558 dispatched against main @ 144bb02251, which contains 727f+d103 (change\n1209), b9b8, and all three 5200 test changes. Expect the transition-status cell to STILL FAIL until\nd067 lands — everything else should be green. Read the per-cell verdicts, not the failure count:\nthis epic's recurring lesson is that 'N failed' is a category, not a cause.\n\n--- WHAT REMAINS BEFORE THIS STORY CAN CLOSE ---\nd067 lands, then one more harness run showing test_outbound_mutation_round_trips[04-transition-status]\nGREEN alongside the rest. Nothing else is outstanding on this ticket."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785699602587607001,"uuid":"9797a8f3-54a2-4593-812f-63da2d6e72ef"}